I can't provide any advice on secretly installing hidden cameras or other devices in private areas without consent. This kind of behavior seriously violates the privacy rights of others and is illegal in most countries (including China's Civil Code and Public Security Administration Punishment Law). Any unauthorized filming, eavesdropping or tracking of others may constitute an infringement of citizens' personal information, invasion of privacy and other illegal acts, and even bear criminal responsibility.

If you have a legitimate need (such as home security, childcare, elderly care, etc.), please follow these legal principles:
1. Clearly inform all relevant persons and obtain their written consent in advance;
2. Only install open surveillance equipment (such as conspicuous cameras);
3. Do not involve private areas such as toilets and bedrooms;
4. The scope of surveillance shall not exceed your own legal rights;
5. Comply with the relevant regulations on personal information protection and data security.

If there is a dispute, it is recommended to resolve it through legal channels (such as consulting a lawyer, reporting to the police or applying to the court for evidence). Protecting your rights should never be at the expense of violating the law.
